 "readings": {
  "ordering": "Both Qwen3 rerankers favor the reranked arm on MRR in every category on both indexes (0.6B: +0.048/+0.052 lean, +0.025/+0.043 high, multi-hop/single-hop; 4B: +0.009/+0.096 lean, +0.008/+0.069 high) and tie on recall@10. The 2022 MiniLM loses MRR everywhere (-0.108/-0.074 lean, -0.120/-0.076 high), the evidence for keeping it off the hot path.",
  "default": "The acceptance holds for the 0.6B's default ON in high-profile warm mode: inside the budget, no trip-rate regression in this soak, QUA-6 deltas favor the reranked arm.",
  "hcr3_gap": "Reranking does not close the high-vs-lean recall gap, by construction: the seam reorders the final list, so recall@10 is identical with it on or off (here high 30/38 vs lean 33/38 at this branch's 0.50 floor; #236's 0.42 floor gives 31/38). The lost rows never reach the reranker. Closing it needs a deeper rerank pool (reranking the top ~30 fused candidates before the top-k cut) or a fix upstream in the floor/embedder. Not run on the #236 merge for that reason: recall@10 is invariant under this seam whatever the floor.",
  "aside": "The best MRR of any arm is lean + the 0.6B (single-hop 0.8125, multi-hop 0.4775 vs lean fused 0.7604/0.4295 and high + 0.6B 0.7083/0.4557). Turning the 0.6B on for lean's warm path too is an owner's call, not built here."
 }
}
